    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "547:2510",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Construction Site",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Construction Site"
        },
        {
          "text": "Building a New School\n\nA new primary school is being built on our street. The construction site has been busy for several months, and I often watch the workers from my bedroom window.\n\nBefore building started, the construction company put up a tall fence around the site with warning signs that said 'Danger — Construction Site — Keep Out' and 'Hard Hats Must Be Worn'. Inside the fence, bulldozers cleared the land and excavators dug deep trenches for the foundations.\n\nThe foundations are the most important part of any building. Workers poured concrete into the trenches and let it set for several days. Once the foundations were solid, they started building the walls using bricks and cement.\n\nA large crane stands in the middle of the site. It lifts heavy steel beams and pallets of bricks to the upper floors. The crane operator sits in a small cabin at the very top — it must be an amazing view!\n\nThe workers wear personal protective equipment: hard hats, high-visibility jackets, steel-toed boots, and sometimes ear protection because of the loud machinery. Safety is very important on a construction site.\n\nI noticed that different workers do different jobs. Bricklayers build the walls, electricians install the wiring, plumbers fit the pipes and water systems, and carpenters work with wood for the doors and window frames.\n\nThe project manager told my father that the school should be finished by next September. I cannot wait to see the completed building. It is fascinating to watch something being built from nothing.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Building a New School A new primary school is being built on our street. The construction site has been busy for several months, and I often watch the workers from my bedroom window. Before building started, the construction company put up a tall fence around the site with warning signs that said 'Danger — Construction Site — Keep Out' and 'Hard Hats Must Be Worn'. Inside the fence, bulldozers cleared the land and excavators dug deep trenches for the foundations. The foundations are the most important part of any building. Workers poured concrete into the trenches and let it set for several days. Once the foundations were solid, they started building the walls using bricks and cement. A large crane stands in the middle of the site. It lifts heavy steel beams and pallets of bricks to the upper floors. The crane operator sits in a small cabin at the very top — it must be an amazing view! The workers wear personal protective equipment: hard hats, high-visibility jackets, steel-toed boots, and sometimes ear protection because of the loud machinery. Safety is very important on a construction site. I noticed that different workers do different jobs. Bricklayers build the walls, electricians install the wiring, plumbers fit the pipes and water systems, and carpenters work with wood for the doors and window frames. The project manager told my father that the school should be finished by next September. I cannot wait to see the completed building. It is fascinating to watch something being built from nothing."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. What safety signs were displayed around the site?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. What safety signs were displayed around the site?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. Why are foundations important?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. Why are foundations important?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What does the crane do on the construction site?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What does the crane do on the construction site?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What protective equipment do the workers wear?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What protective equipment do the workers wear?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. Name three types of construction workers mentioned in the text.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. Name three types of construction workers mentioned in the text."
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "547:2523",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "build from the ground up",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "build from the ground up"
        },
        {
          "text": "create something from nothing",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "create something from nothing"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"They built the company from the ground up.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"They built the company from the ground up.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "lay the foundations",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "lay the foundations"
        },
        {
          "text": "establish the basis for something",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "establish the basis for something"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Good reading habits lay the foundations for academic success.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"Good reading habits lay the foundations for academic success.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "hit the nail on the head",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "hit the nail on the head"
        },
        {
          "text": "say or do exactly the right thing",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "say or do exactly the right thing"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"You hit the nail on the head with that answer.\"",
